---
import { href } from '../../i18n';
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { contactEmail } from '../../shared/contact';

/*
 * Privacy notice (English). Keep in sync with src/pages/privacidad.astro. Not reviewed by a lawyer.
 * Pending from the client: legal name and address of the controller (today only "Soul Matcha").
 */
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Soul Matcha handles the information of people who visit this site and of people who write to us."
  updated="October 29, 2026"
  routeKey="privacy"
>
  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>
    This site is informational. It has no forms, user accounts, purchases or
    comments, and it does not store personal data about the people who visit it.
    The only way to contact us is by email: below we explain what happens with
    the data you send us when you write to us.
  </p>

  <h2>Data controller</h2>
  <p>
    Soul Matcha is the controller of the personal data you send us by email. You
    can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What data we handle</h2>
  <p>
    Only what you send us when you write to us: your email address, your name if
    you include it, and the content of your message. We do not ask for sensitive
    personal data (for example, health, ethnic origin or religion): please do
    not include it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we use it for</h2>
  <p>
    To answer your inquiry, for example about wholesale, partnerships or
    locations, and to follow up on it. We do not use it for advertising or to
    build profiles.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your data or share it with third parties for their own
    purposes. Your messages go through the email service provider we use, which
    processes them to deliver and store them. We could also share them if a
    competent authority requires it under the law.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    For as long as needed to handle your inquiry and its follow-up, and as
    required by applicable legal obligations. After that we delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can access your data, rectify it, cancel it or object to its processing
    (ARCO rights), and you can also withdraw your consent or limit the use of
    your data. To exercise them, write to us at{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> from the same email
    address you used to contact us, say which right you want to exercise and
    which data it involves. We will reply within the deadlines set by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you believe your rights were not respected, you can go to the competent
    data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Consent</h2>
  <p>
    By writing to us we understand that you accept this notice for the purposes
    described. You can withdraw your consent at any time by writing to the same
    email address.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do on the site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not use analytics or measurement tools.</li>
    <li>We do not use advertising or tracking pixels.</li>
    <li>
      We do not embed third-party videos or social media buttons. The video on
      the home page is served from this same site. The only third-party content
      is the Google map on the locations page, and it loads only when you press
      “Show map”: until then, Google is not contacted.
    </li>
    <li>
      We do not load any other resources from other domains: fonts, images and
      video are served from this same site.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Technical data from hosting</h2>
  <p>
    This site is hosted on GitHub Pages and published at soulmatcha.com. As with
    any web server, the host may log technical data about each visit (for
    example, the IP address, browser and date) for security and operational
    purposes. We do not access or use those logs. To see how they are handled,
    read the host's{' '}
    <a
      href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      target="_blank"
    >
      GitHub privacy statement
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <p>If we change hosting provider, we will update this notice.</p>

  <h2>Storage in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The site stores a few technical items in your browser in order to work. They
    contain no personal information. See the details on the{' '}
    <a href={href('cookies', 'en')}>cookies page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to Instagram, Uber Eats and Google Maps. When you open them
    you leave this site and their own privacy policies apply, separate from this
    notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>
    If the site starts to collect data through other means (for example, a
    contact form or analytics), we will update this notice beforehand and, where
    applicable, ask for your consent. The date above shows the latest revision.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
